# Per-profile secrets for Hermes profile kevin.
# Copy names to live ~/.hermes/profiles/kevin/.env after install (or fill when Hermes prompts).
# API keys and tokens set here override the shell environment.
# Behavioral settings belong in config.yaml, not here.
#
# Do NOT commit a real .env. This template ships names only.
# Path of record: docs/runbooks/kevin-auth-packaging.md
#
# Two credential modes (one working path is enough):
#   Path A — API keys below in live .env (or hermes -p kevin auth add <provider> --type api-key)
#   Path B — OAuth / subscription pool: hermes -p kevin auth … → live auth.json (never commit)
# See kevin-auth-packaging for second-operator fill + smoke and never-copy guardrails.

# --- Core provider API keys (Path A; all optional if Path B covers the default provider) ---
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# --- Optional terminal env export for sandboxed shells (example name only) ---
# TERMINAL_ENV=

# --- Slack (Socket Mode) — owned by KEVN-8; names only cross-ref ---
# Not a complete Slack packaging story. Prefer packs/factory-slack.env.example and KEVN-8
# kevin-scoped docs when they land. Do not treat this block as ownership of Slack packaging.
# Put values only in live ~/.hermes/profiles/kevin/.env — never commit tokens.
# SLACK_BOT_TOKEN=
# SLACK_APP_TOKEN=
# SLACK_ALLOWED_USERS=
# SLACK_ALLOWED_CHANNELS=
# SLACK_HOME_CHANNEL=
